{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{Rings}$", "MATH_0002": "$1$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Rings}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1faefc9b689937ba2644e9c1a62d7ed4eccb5138cdc328c213b41a3348aaf372", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:224369d94d0faa1349dafc2a43f37d700654ad83e8e2e6dcee3859f0699bee3d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that <MATH_0001> denotes the category of commutative rings\nwith <MATH_0002>. For an object <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004> we denote <MATH_0005>\nthe category of <MATH_0006>-modules.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b836533b57ffcdb835077c859b763242403023671e71c9adb8089de43f75154", "unit_id": "tag:08WJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$f : R \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\bullet \\otimes_R S: \\text{Mod}_R \\to \\text{Mod}_S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{homology-section-functors}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-reflects}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:93370aaad8eceeec0d451da28226e89408912bb3aef897bc627ae30a6705694c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:43ba713d46da807d8bc81732342453fad7f13b571d72468167f78878dcbcdbec", "source_text": "Any functor <MATH_0001> of abelian categories\nwhich is exact and takes nonzero objects to nonzero objects reflects\ninjections and surjections. Namely, exactness implies that\n<MATH_0002> preserves kernels and cokernels (compare with\nHomology, Section <REF_0001>).\nFor example, if <MATH_0003> is a \nfaithfully flat ring homomorphism, then\n<MATH_0004> has these properties.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d454107ef5e5951c922bbd356ea3452d85f9e6bcc3a86ddae5051d4d8395d107", "unit_id": "tag:08WK:statement"}
